{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"broadish-permanent-condor","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\nThe box fixture in tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_review_drain.py constructs env = dict(os.environ) and returns that mapping inside the fixture value. When a test fails, pytest renders the fixture argument and can print ambient credential values into local or CI logs. This was directly observed during a deliberate defect-seeded RED run; no credential value is recorded on this ticket. The performance ticket must not absorb an unrelated security fix.\n\n## Plan\n- Reproduce with a synthetic sentinel secret in the ambient environment and a deliberate assertion failure.\n- Change the fixture boundary to pass only required environment variables or use a representation-safe wrapper while preserving the real bash subprocess environment needed by the tests.\n- Audit sibling subprocess fixtures for the same dict(os.environ)-inside-rendered-fixture shape.\n- Prove the synthetic sentinel never appears in pytest failure output while the autodeploy suite remains behaviorally green.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A deterministic regression test fails before the fix because a synthetic ambient secret appears in captured pytest failure rendering.\n- [ ] The synthetic secret is absent from failure output after the fix.\n- [ ] Required PATH and autodeploy environment behavior remains covered through the real bash subprocess.\n- [ ] Sibling occurrences are inventoried and either fixed or linked as follow-ups.\n- [ ] Repository gates and Gerrit votes pass before closure.","id":"fc43-3c50-ec6c-4a3e","parent_id":"","priority":1,"tags":["security","tests"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Prevent autodeploy test failures from printing ambient credentials"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786832134098619001,"uuid":"bc2248b3-3720-407f-a567-e3364b15e7fa"}